<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεμπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blameless, without reproach,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				342
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέμπτους ὑμᾶς ἐδείξατε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.216
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. χρόνου</span> in regard of
			time, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				692
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τἆλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					521
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					629
				</span></i>
			(dub.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ὑπὸ τῶν φίλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					6.8
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἐκείνῃ</span>
			<i>without blame</i> to her, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				35
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερος</span>”
				<i>less blameworthy,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of things,
				<i>perfect in its kind,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖπνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					2.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					945d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πάντα ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					3.10.2
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				<i>irreproachably,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					269
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1465
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.3.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.64
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not blaming, well content,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεμπτόν τινα ποιεῖν</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.5.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.4.28
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, δέχεσθαί τινα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.2.37
			</span></i>.</div>
